  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4. See Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements are presented in accordance with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles as well as the Uniform System of Accounts prescribed by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). Accordingly, they do not include all the information and footnotes required for the annual report. In the opinion of management, all adjustments (consisting of normal and recurring accruals) considered necessary for a fair presentation have been included. Operating results for the six-month period ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 are not necessarily indicative of the results that may be expected and ultimately realized for the year ending December 31, 2026. The interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and accompanying notes of Colonial Pipeline ("Colonial" or "the Company") presented in the 2025 Form 6 Annual Report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Legal Contingencies and Environmental Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Matters Pertaining to Customer Actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 1, 2024, one of Colonial's shippers filed a new complaint with the FERC asserting that the Company's indexed rates are unjust and unreasonable and further challenging the Company's market-based rates. Five additional shippers subsequently filed similar complaints. On April 2, 2025, the FERC issued an order consolidating the six complaints that were outstanding as of that date into one proceeding (Docket No. OR24-3). With that order, the FERC also dismissed the challenges to Colonial's market-based rates and referred the challenges to the indexed rates to a hearing process, suspending that hearing process pending a FERC settlement process. On May 23, 2025, a seventh shipper filed a complaint (Docket No. OR25-8). On September 24, 2025, this shipper's complaint was consolidated into the same proceeding as the previously filed six complaints. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 4, 2026, an order was issued terminating the settlement procedures and designating a presiding administrative law judge. The FERC assigned the complaint to a Track 3 schedule, reserved for complex cases. The order established that the hearing must be convened within 42 weeks, and the initial decision must be issued within 63 weeks. On July 31, 2026, an order was issued to extend this schedule by four months. As of the date of this report, Colonial has settled with certain shippers. Colonial has substantial defenses to these complaints and will vigorously assert these defenses. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;FERC Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The FERC indexing system provides for annual index rate adjustments effective no earlier than July 1st of each year. The indexing system currently applies to a majority of the Company&#8217;s published tariff rates. Colonial elected to adjust its index rates in each of the periods presented within this report in keeping with the FERC indexing system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 20, 2025, the FERC issued a Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (NOPR) to seek comment on a proposed index level used to determine annual changes to oil pipeline rate ceilings for the five-year period commencing on July 1, 2026. The FERC proposed to use the Producer Price Index for Finished Goods (PPI-FG) minus 1.42% as the index level for the five-year period. Comments to this NOPR were submitted. On April 24, 2026, the FERC issued a final rule establishing a new oil pipeline index level of PPI-FG minus 0.55% for the five-year period commencing July 1, 2026. This rule is subject to appeal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Colonial has evaluated events occurring subsequent to the balance sheet date but prior to September&#160;8, 2026, the date the financial statements were available for issuance, that would have a material impact on these Form 6-Q financial statements. Such events have been properly disclosed in the accompanying notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
